WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.836 --> 00:00:03.317
"Hi! I heard you guys are detectives."

2
00:00:03.897 --> 00:00:08.140
Henry glanced up from pouring a cup of lemonade.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:17.925
So did his cousin, Maggie, and his best friend, Cole.

4
00:00:29.832 --> 00:00:34.496
It was a hot summer day in Belltown, and the kids' lemonade stand was busy.

5
00:00:36.097 --> 00:00:37.939
A girl named Gail was standing there.

6
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.384
Gail was a year ahead of Henry and Cole in school and three years ahead of Maggie.

7
00:00:43.404 --> 00:00:46.807
"Yes, we are detectives!"

8
00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.048
Maggie told her.

9
00:00:48.068 --> 00:00:51.711
"We solve all mysteries, large and small.

10
00:00:52.591 --> 00:00:53.552
See our new sign?"

11
00:00:54.413 --> 00:00:57.736
There were two handmade signs hanging by the lemonade stand.

12
00:00:58.676 --> 00:01:00.637
The first sign was about the lemonade.

13
00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:04.219
The second sign was about the stand's latest business.

14
00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:15.184
It said: The Lemonade Detectives All Mysteries Solved, Guaranteed No Problem Too Large or Too Small $5 per

15
00:01:15.224 --> 00:01:23.067
case plus expenses Henry thought the new sign looked great, but so far it hadn't brought any customers

16
00:01:23.127 --> 00:01:24.508
with mysteries to solve.

17
00:01:26.144 --> 00:01:31.306
The other sign, however, had brought plenty of people looking for a cold glass of lemonade.

18
00:01:31.326 --> 00:01:33.447
"Do you have a mystery for us?"

19
00:01:33.907 --> 00:01:35.328
Cole asked Gail eagerly.

20
00:01:35.348 --> 00:01:42.471
"No, my sister just told me that you three are detectives now," Gail said.

21
00:01:42.491 --> 00:01:45.312
"I'd like to buy some lemonade though."

22
00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.753
Maggie looked disappointed.

23
00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:51.034
"Are you sure you don't have a case for us?

24
00:01:52.115 --> 00:01:54.856
Hasn't anything mysterious happened to you lately?"

25
00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:58.329
"Nope. Sorry," Gail said.

26
00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.730
Henry reached for the lemonade pitcher.

27
00:02:01.991 --> 00:02:04.772
He poured some into a cup and handed the cup to Gail.

28
00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:09.014
"That will be 25 cents, please," he told her.

29
00:02:09.034 --> 00:02:10.955
"Enjoy your lemonade."

30
00:02:10.975 --> 00:02:14.397
"Thanks." Gail handed him a quarter.

31
00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:17.659
"Good luck with your detective agency."

32
00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:20.300
After she left, Henry sighed.

33
00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:25.684
"I'm starting to think that there are no more mysteries to solve in Belltown."

34
00:02:25.704 --> 00:02:30.387
"We've been sitting here all morning, and haven't gotten a single case!"

35
00:02:30.888 --> 00:02:31.548
Cole added.

36
00:02:31.568 --> 00:02:34.791
"We could have been playing soccer instead."

37
00:02:34.811 --> 00:02:37.273
"At least we're making money."

38
00:02:38.294 --> 00:02:40.015
Maggie fanned herself with her hand.

39
00:02:40.035 --> 00:02:44.579
"It won't be long before I have enough to start horseback-riding lessons!"

40
00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:50.204
Maggie had started the lemonade stand because she wanted to take riding lessons.

41
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.361
Her parents had told her they would only pay half the cost.

42
00:02:55.402 --> 00:02:58.343
She needed to earn enough money to pay the other half herself.

43
00:02:59.324 --> 00:03:02.365
The lemonade stand was a success right from the start.

44
00:03:03.385 --> 00:03:06.667
Maggie had made plenty of money selling her delicious lemonade.

45
00:03:07.927 --> 00:03:11.369
But then all her money had disappeared right out of her cashbox!

46
00:03:12.389 --> 00:03:14.950
Henry and Cole had helped her track down the thief.

47
00:03:15.871 --> 00:03:18.872
That was when the idea for The Lemonade Detectives was born.

48
00:03:19.872 --> 00:03:23.674
"We'd be making a lot more money if we had a case," Cole grumbled.

49
00:03:23.694 --> 00:03:27.955
"Besides Henry and I never agreed to be lemonade salesmen.

50
00:03:29.196 --> 00:03:30.416
We want to be detectives!"

51
00:03:32.177 --> 00:03:35.999
"Detectives need to be patient," Maggie shot back.

52
00:03:36.939 --> 00:03:43.162
"Sooner or later we'll get a case and then—" "Stop arguing, you two," Henry said.

53
00:03:43.182 --> 00:03:45.763
"Here come some more customers."

54
00:03:46.723 --> 00:03:48.564
A group of boys was heading their way.

55
00:03:49.484 --> 00:03:53.746
"Four lemonades, please," one boy said, holding out a dollar bill.

56
00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.767
"Here you go."

57
00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:57.847
Maggie poured their lemonade.

58
00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:02.750
"Did you know that we offer detective services now as well as lemonade?"

59
00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.871
The first boy squinted at the new sign.

60
00:04:05.891 --> 00:04:09.072
"How can you guys be detectives?"

61
00:04:09.532 --> 00:04:10.113
he asked.

62
00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:12.193
"You're just kids."

63
00:04:13.214 --> 00:04:17.796
A boy named Ryan, who never went anywhere without his skateboard, was standing there too.

64
00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.523
"I bet it's because they figured out who stole Maggie's money," he said.

65
00:04:23.543 --> 00:04:26.325
"They thought it was me at first!"

66
00:04:27.305 --> 00:04:32.849
He began telling his friends about how he'd been a suspect as the boys walked away sipping their

67
00:04:32.889 --> 00:04:39.133
lemonade. "At least people are hearing about our detective agency," Maggie said, watching them go.

68
00:04:39.153 --> 00:04:42.275
"That's good," Henry said.

69
00:04:42.295 --> 00:04:47.339
"But I don't think all three of us need to stay here for the whole day."

70
00:04:47.359 --> 00:04:49.020
Cole nodded.

71
00:04:49.964 --> 00:04:53.286
"Henry and I could go play soccer, and you could call us if someone shows up with a

72
00:04:53.327 --> 00:04:56.429
mystery." "No way!"

73
00:04:56.889 --> 00:04:57.490
Maggie said.

74
00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:00.352
"I need you to help me with the lemonade."

75
00:05:00.372 --> 00:05:06.776
"If we aren't here, it means you get to keep all the lemonade money," Henry reminded her.

76
00:05:07.777 --> 00:05:09.958
Maggie hesitated, thinking about that.

77
00:05:09.978 --> 00:05:15.142
"Here comes your next lemonade customer, Maggie," Cole said, pointing down the street.

78
00:05:16.483 --> 00:05:17.284
"He's all yours."

79
00:05:18.528 --> 00:05:20.790
Henry glanced at the boy hurrying toward them.

80
00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:24.533
"Hey, it's Nathan," he said.

81
00:05:24.553 --> 00:05:27.996
"Maybe we should see if he wants to play soccer with us."

82
00:05:29.037 --> 00:05:32.480
Nathan was a kid in Henry and Cole's class who lived nearby.

83
00:05:33.481 --> 00:05:37.024
Everyone liked him because he was always friendly, nice, and happy.

84
00:05:38.325 --> 00:05:42.728
When he got closer, though, Henry saw that Nathan didn't look very happy right now.

85
00:05:43.789 --> 00:05:46.452
In fact, he was frowning and looking worried.

86
00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:48.501
"What's up, Nathan?"

87
00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:51.303
Cole asked when Nathan reached the lemonade stand.

88
00:05:52.464 --> 00:05:56.868
Nathan pulled a five-dollar bill out of his pocket and slapped it down on the table.

89
00:05:56.888 --> 00:05:59.670
"I've got a mystery for you!"

90
00:06:00.511 --> 00:06:01.032
he announced.
